# Pairs with NoStrandedPrepare. The broadcast declares the saga done once ANY
# participant has applied its terminal rather than once every one has, so the
# rest are never told. Every saga still reaches "done", so Termination stays
# green, and a stranded bucket under a reported commit still reads post-saga
# through the gate, so EveryCommittedKeyReadable stays green too. That is the
# point of the pairing: it is a protocol defect under the fairness Spec
# actually asserts, and of the liveness properties only NoStrandedPrepare can
# see it (issue #2321).
MODULE: NoStrandedPrepareEarlyCompletion
TARGET: NoStrandedPrepare
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: completes the saga after the first participant's terminal, so the remaining participants are never told
PERTURBS: BroadcastStep

--- FIND
           allDone == \A j \in Written(t) : nterm[j] # "none"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: "some participant applied its terminal" is mistaken for "every
\* participant did", so the saga leaves the broadcast phase early.
           allDone == \E j \in Written(t) : nterm[j] # "none"
--- END
